{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Getting Started with Cogni AI Agentic Collections",
  "description": "Walkthrough of the repository for AI agent skills, agents, workflows, devcontainer, and Waza validation. Covers devcontainer build fixes, skill standards, CI workflows, and contribution.",
  "isPrimary": true,
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Welcome to Cogni AI Agentic Collections!",
      "description": "# Welcome! \ud83e\udd16\n\nThis repository is the organization-wide collection of AI agent personas, skills, plugins, instructions, and workflows for tools like GitHub Copilot, Claude, OpenCode, and Waza.\n\n## What You'll Learn\n- Devcontainer setup (jammy image, provision.yml with Ansible, MCP, NO_COLOR for clean logs)\n- Skill standard (`SKILL.md` with Waza validation, <500 tokens, triggers, USE FOR/DO NOT USE FOR)\n- Agentic workflows (`gh aw`, waza checks, summary generation)\n- Coding standards and pre-commit\n- How changes to devcontainer/SKILL.md/workflows affect CI\n\nThe recent fixes addressed devcontainer build (sudo usage, noble->jammy), Waza compliance in SKILL.md, and escape sequences in logs for summary action.",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Devcontainer Configuration",
      "description": "## Reproducible Dev Environment\n\nThe `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` now uses the stable `mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/base:jammy` image (matching the org's `.github` repo). Key updates:\n- `onCreateCommand`: Bootstrap with `sudo apt-get` + `ansible-playbook .devcontainer/provision.yml` (installs tools, pipx Ansible, Copilot CLI, Cogni plugins, pre-commit).\n- Features: python, github-cli, docker-in-docker, opencode, eget, actionlint, vim, make.\n- `postCreateCommand`: eget for CLI tools (bat, rg, yq, + minizinc/rga).\n- VS Code: extensions, MCP GitHub server, terminal profile.\n- `initializeCommand`: Pre-creates OpenCode host dirs for bind mounts.\n\n**Fixes applied**: Switched from noble build to avoid sudo/docker issues; added NO_COLOR env in workflows; condensed skills for Waza.\n\nRun `devcontainer rebuild` after changes.",
      "file": ".devcontainer/devcontainer.json",
      "line": 4
    },
    {
      "title": "Provision Playbook",
      "description": "## Ansible Provisioning\n\n`.devcontainer/provision.yml` handles post-bootstrap setup (apt from `apt-packages.txt`, pipx Ansible + inject for docker/requests, Python reqs, Copilot CLI, gh copilot marketplace/plugins for cogni-ai-*, pre-commit hooks).\n\nUpdated inject task uses `pipx inject` with improved idempotency (matches org `.github` version).\n\nSee `requirements-ansible.txt` and `requirements.txt` for deps. This ensures no extra venvs (per project rules) and controller-side deps are in devcontainer.",
      "file": ".devcontainer/provision.yml",
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Skill Standard & Waza",
      "description": "## SKILL.md Compliance\n\nSkills follow the `agentskills` open standard (see `.agents/skills/agentskills/SKILL.md`).\n\n**Recent fix** (for PR #133): Condensed `plugins/cogni-ai-dev-ops/skills/devcontainer/SKILL.md`:\n- Expanded frontmatter `description` (>150 chars + triggers).\n- Added `metadata` for provenance.\n- Standard headings (When to Use, When Not to Use, Core Principles, Common Pitfalls).\n- Minimal example; removed long embedded JSON (now references the file).\n- Token count now <500; added Waza reference.\n\nWaza (`waza check`) enforces this in CI (`waza-check.yml`). Run locally with Go 1.26+: `waza check plugins/cogni-ai-dev-ops/skills/devcontainer`.\n\nUse `agent-skill-md-writer` skill when editing SKILL.md.",
      "file": "plugins/cogni-ai-dev-ops/skills/devcontainer/SKILL.md",
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Agentic Workflows & CI",
      "description": "## GitHub Agentic Workflows (gh aw)\n\n- `cogni-ai-agent.yml`: Triggers on PRs/comments; runs agents (cogni-ai-coder, architect, etc.); uses cloned agents/instructions/skills repos.\n- `waza-check.yml`: Validates changed SKILL.md/*.agent.md on PR/push; fails on non-compliance; generates summary.\n- `waza-check-pr-comment.yml`: Posts results as PR comment.\n- Added `NO_COLOR=1` + `TERM=dumb` to jobs to fix summary parser (no ANSI escapes).\n\n**Fix applied**: Env vars prevent \"terminal escape sequences\" error in `ai-inference/summary` action.\n\nSee `.github/workflows/README.md` for details. Use `gh aw` for agentic tasks.",
      "file": ".github/workflows/cogni-ai-agent.yml",
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Coding Standards & Pre-commit",
      "description": "## Quality Gates\n\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml`: yamllint, markdownlint, ansible-lint, codespell, gitleaks, etc.\n- `.github/copilot-instructions.md`: Python (uv, PEP8, argparse, BrokenPipeError), JSON/YAML/Markdown rules, devcontainer guidance (no extra venvs, use container Python, update requirements for missing deps).\n- `AGENTS.md`, `AGENTS-RUNTIME.md`, skills in `.agents/skills/` and `plugins/*/skills/`.\n\nRun `pre-commit run -a` locally. CI enforces on PRs.\n\n**Tour update**: This file was refreshed to reflect devcontainer fixes, Waza, condensed skills, and NO_COLOR env.",
      "file": ".pre-commit-config.yaml",
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Contribution Workflow",
      "description": "## How to Contribute\n\n1. Update skill/agent or devcontainer (keep tours current!).\n2. `pre-commit run -a` + `waza check` on SKILL.md changes.\n3. PR with description; Waza + Cogni AI Agent + summary will run.\n4. Address CodeRabbit/Sourcery reviews.\n5. Merge on green checks.\n\nSee `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `docs/` for more. Use the agents (cogni-ai-coder, dev-ops, etc.) via comments or `gh aw`.\n\nThis tour is kept up-to-date per project rules after devcontainer/SKILL/workflow changes.",
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 30
    }
  ]
}